#pragma once
namespace UnmadeCore {
struct DepthSpec{const char* quest;const char* goal;const char* offer;const char* witness;const char* evidence;const char* option_a;const char* option_b;const char* return_a;const char* return_b;const char* challenge;const char* secret_name;const char* power;const char* counterparty;const char* witness_return_a;const char* witness_return_b;const char* public_return_a;const char* public_return_b;};
inline constexpr DepthSpec DepthSpecs[]={
{"The Last Lantern Charter","Choose which road the surviving lantern charter will serve.","A charter says every traveler is welcome. Last winter we counted beds instead. Jessa kept the names I stopped writing.","I kept those names because a missing name becomes an empty bed. Maelin wants the lanterns on the road; I want somebody to admit who was left outside.","The torn charter lists both the abandoned beds and a reserve of lantern oil. Neither claim cancels the other.","Keep the lantern reserve on the refuge road","Publish the excluded names and reserve the archive room","We will keep a bed ready. Jessa still asks why the list is folded shut.","The names are posted. I have moved a lantern indoors; the outer road will need your field kit.","Ring the road bells 1, 3, 2","A lantern hidden behind the charter panel","Marked Opening","Charter Enforcer","I will keep checking the list. A warm bed does not make an excluded name disappear.","Now I can point to the names instead of asking somebody to believe my memory. I still have to find them beds.","The refuge-road lanterns remain lit through the night, but the folded exclusion list has not been posted. There is still work for the shelter.","Names of those denied beds now hang in the archive room; one road lantern was moved indoors, leaving the outer route less certain."},
{"Water For Those Still Waiting","Decide who controls the recovered pump schedule.","The pump schedule is ours again. Havin says the drywake families should hold it. I have watched strangers arrive with nothing but empty cups.","An open pump is a promise until somebody drinks it dry. Give the families a protected hour. Leave the rest of the day open.","A soaked schedule shows the pumps stopped before the tanks were empty. A private water hour could preserve a reserve or become another gate.","Guarantee a protected family water hour","Keep access public and post every withdrawal","Havin keeps the protected hour. The provisioner charges less; travelers wait until the bell.","The withdrawal sheet is public. We spend more time checking it, but newcomers can ask for water.","Set pump switches 1 and 3; confirm during the low-water interval","A saltglass lens beneath the dry walkway","Pressure Read","Brine Syndic","My household knows when the pump is ours. I will be the one explaining the wait to the next stranger.","I will bring our cups at the public hour. If the withdrawal sheet is wrong, I want my name beside the correction.","A family water hour is marked on the harbor bell. Travelers now wait through the protected interval before they can draw from the shared pump.","Every pump withdrawal is posted where the harbor can inspect it. Newcomers can ask for water, but the public accounting takes time."},
{"The Heat Left Over","Decide where the recovered heat should go.","The holding room had heat while the refuge did not. Ilyet has measured the pipes. We can warm the houses or keep a reserve for the next rescue.","A rescue reserve sounds humane until every cold night is called temporary. I can reroute the pipe, but I will not pretend one valve warms everyone.","A service diagram separates the domestic line from a guarded emergency reservoir. Both share the same limited intake.","Warm the refuge houses first","Keep a rescue reserve with a public meter","The houses are warm. Ilyet checks the reserve before agreeing to send a crew underground.","The meter is where everyone can read it. The houses keep their blankets; the rescue crew keeps its heat.","Touch all three cooling relays within eighteen seconds","An insulated forge grip beyond the cooling panel","Ember Counter","Reservoir Keeper","I measured the house line this morning. It is warm. I am also measuring what remains for a rescue.","The rescue meter is honest. It does not make the refuge warmer, and I will not stop saying that.","The refuge houses have warmth again; crews still measure the smaller reserve before agreeing to another underground rescue.","The rescue meter stands in public view and the rescue heat is kept back. Some families remain cold while the emergency crew prepares."},
{"Whose Oath Remains","Decide how the surviving debt oath will be held.","Velka is my name. The ledger knows me as a guarantor. Deyra found a margin where the collector wrote that I would pay for strangers I had never met.","The margin is real. So is the promise Velka made to two families. Destroying a forced oath must not erase the promise they still rely on.","A copied oath distinguishes the voluntary family promise from the collector's added liability. The ink layers can be read separately.","Keep the family promise and seal the forced margin","Expose the whole oath and renegotiate it publicly","The families still have a guarantor. Deyra keeps the sealed copy so the margin cannot return unnoticed.","The oath is being read aloud. Some people trust us more; others will not wait for the negotiation.","Enable weights 1 and 2 for a total load of five","A witness clasp in the counterweight recess","Oath Interrupt","Margin Collector","The forced margin is sealed separately. I kept a second copy so nobody can quietly join it to the promise again.","People can read the whole oath now. We still need to say which promise we will actually keep.","The two families still have a guarantor; the added forced debt margin is sealed separately, so the old collector cannot silently claim it.","The complete oath is read openly at the pier. Negotiations continue, and people cannot yet count on a settlement to arrive."},
{"A Voice On The Bridge","Choose the obligation that the restored span will carry.","The span can hold workers again. Kelm wants the choir anchor returned to it. The anchor steadies the bridge, but it also decides whose footsteps count.","I can hear every crossing in the anchor. That is why I want it restored and why Liora wants the record open. Safety has become a way to listen without asking.","The anchor records footsteps as well as load. Its structural use does not require retaining a named crossing record.","Restore the anchor and limit access to its record","Open the crossing record and use manual load watches","The anchor carries the weight. Kelm answers for the locked record; the watch still counts every load.","The record is open. Liora has asked for another watcher, because reading it does not hold a bridge up.","Reach the upper walkway and ground all three wind anchors","A choirweight hook on the high ledge","Grounded Fold","Anchor Auditor","The anchor is carrying the span. Its locked record is my responsibility, not permission to listen whenever I please.","I have taken a manual load watch. Reading the crossing record will not hold the bridge up for me.","The choir anchor steadies the bridge, while its records remain restricted and every load still needs a responsible watch.","Footstep records are open to inspection and manual load watchers now cover the bridge. Knowing who crossed does not make the span safer."},
{"The Name In The Seam","Decide what to do with an ancestor record found in the foundry.","Seyl's family name is under a seam the claimant called unworked. I can protect their claim by sealing the copy. Seyl wants to know who else was buried beside it.","Aren can keep our claim safe. I still want the other names read. I do not want to inherit a house that depends on keeping another family invisible.","The seam copy carries a family claim and several neighboring names. The claimant's stamp covers both, rather than establishing either as false.","Protect the family claim in a sealed local trust","Publish the neighboring names with the claim","The local trust holds the copy. Seyl visits the seam because the other names have not stopped mattering.","The neighboring names are on the wall. Aren has had to defend our claim in front of people it once excluded.","Lock the memory shutters 1, 2, 3","A seamfinder tooth behind the stopped shutter","Seam Read","Seam Evictor","Our claim is protected. I am still asking what happened to the neighboring names under the seal.","I read the neighbors' names aloud. Some families have answered, and we will have to make room for their claims.","The family's claim is preserved in a sealed trust. The neighboring names in the same stone remain unresolved rather than erased.","The neighboring names are displayed beside the family claim, drawing other households to ask whose work and home were overlooked."},
{"Names For A Safe House","Decide how rescued people will appear in the local census.","Ovin can write the people we rescued into the census. That would make their beds visible to the storekeeper. It would also make their names visible to anyone asking.","I have a blank page and a real storehouse. An unnamed household can be starved politely. A named household can be found by someone it fears.","The storehouse sheet accepts household totals without personal names. An attached index would identify each person if it were retained.","Register household totals and seal personal names","Register names openly with an appeal witness","The storehouse has the totals. Ovin keeps the name page sealed and has promised to ask before opening it.","The names have a witness beside them. Neris is still making sure nobody mistakes an appeal for permission.","Read all three lamps while unobserved; crouch or clear the patrol","An unlisted cloak pin under the census stair","Unlisted Step","Index Hunter","The storekeeper has a household total. The personal page will stay sealed until somebody gives permission to open it.","I wrote the appeal beside every name. I expect to be called when somebody tries to ignore it.","Storehouse staff count the rescued households without displaying personal names. The separate name page is still sealed until consent.","An appeal witness stands beside the open census record. Being written in the index does not mean a person has surrendered a right to object."},
{"The Branch They Did Not Graft","Decide who may harvest the restored root passage.","The root passage is open. Alva found an old boundary cut through the graft. The old claim would keep the harvest safe for one household.","My household has eaten from that root for years. I will not call the claim fair just because it fed us. Sivra thinks a common harvest can survive without a keeper.","A root marker names the household boundary; a later tool mark widens it across the common path. The two cuts were made in different seasons.","Keep the household boundary with a public harvest share","Restore the common path and appoint rotating keepers","The household boundary stays. Alva leaves a share at the common post, where everyone can see whether it arrived.","The path is common again. Sivra takes the first watch and cannot ask Alva to carry every hungry season alone.","Grow the root controls 3, 1, 2","A commonbark graft charm beyond the root bridge","Root Counter","Boundary Hewer","I put the public share at the post myself. My household cannot call it a gift and then take it back unseen.","The common path is open. I have a watch hour, and so does Sivra. That is how I will know we meant it.","The household boundary remains and a harvest share is left at the common post where everyone can check whether it arrived.","The root passage is common again; rotating keepers now share the watch so the same gardener does not carry every lean season."},
{"The Door We Can Describe","Decide how to record the reopened threshold.","Essel can describe the threshold we have crossed. We can seal that description for the next rescue, or let travelers read it. A description is not an answer to what began this place.","I will write where we put our hands and what opened. I will not write that we understand the absence. Thaelin worries people will treat a route as a promise.","The threshold diagram records a working passage and two untested side doors. It explicitly leaves the origin of the first absence unknown.","Keep the working route in a rescue registry","Publish the route with the untested doors marked","The rescue registry holds the route. Essel left the untested doors in the drawing instead of pretending they were gone.","The route is public, with its uncertainty intact. Thaelin asks every traveler to read the warning before choosing.","Enable boundary mirrors 2 and 3; leave mirror 1 dark","A threshold brace inside the untested alcove","Nearness Hold","Registry Sealkeeper","The rescue registry has the working route. The untested doors are still drawn as untested.","The traveler can read the route and its warning together. I have written no answer about where the absence began.","The working rescue route is recorded in a restricted registry; two untested doors remain marked as unknown, not solved.","Travelers can read the public threshold map, including warnings for the untested side doors and a passage that still needs judgment."},
};
}
